      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If a shader has odd lighting from incorrect vertex normals (or that data is used for another purpose) then it's the responsibility of the shader author to include the appropriate keywords in their shader name so it appears as unlit or the Ramp property with a blank value. Emission has nothing to do with lighting issues as it is a fundamentally different system (emissive objects are unit by definition).",
      "viewerReactions": null
