  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-04T23:21:00.994Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm noticing a lot of models being rolled back are suffering hard in how they are lit. A lot of models have weird face shading or strange patchy lit spots on their face where vertexes aren't quite right, while this is on the model makes to make neater models, also adding a way to pass an emission value to the standard shader would make a lot of people's lives a lot easier.",
